<title>UK: Industrial Control year pretax profit surges.</title>
<headline>Industrial Control year pretax profit surges.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to May 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		9.03 profit	  vs 2.03 loss</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 3.6		    vs 3.6</p>
<p> Pretax		     5.56		   vs 0.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   77.06		  vs 83.80</p>
<p>NOTE - UK high-technology electronic equipment company Industrial Controls Services Group Plc said that following a major restructuring it was now a &quot;totally focused group&quot;. Order books were greatly increased compated with last year, it added.</p>
<p> Operating profit	 7.33		   vs 5.85</p>
<p> Tax charge		 1.68		   vs 0.55</p>
<p> Net taxed		  3.89		   vs 0.45</p>
<p> Retained result	  2.14 profit	  vs 2.29 loss</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 15</p>
<p>Div registration date  Oct 1  Ex-div date		Sept 23</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7972</p>
